"槓桿與償債","desc":"股本未遭稀釋 (ΔShares ≤ 0)","passed":1,"detail":"未大幅增發新股割韭菜"},{"id":8,"category":"營運效率","desc":"毛利率擴張 (ΔMargin > 0)","passed":0,"detail":"產品定價權增強，毛利結構健康"},{"id":9,"category":"營運效率","desc":"資產週轉率提升 (ΔTurnover > 0)","passed":0,"detail":"每單位資產產出效益改善"}],"fair_val":52.3,"default_fair_val":52.3,"premium_pct":-42.1,"is_undervalued":true,"pe_trailing":23.4,"pe_forward":20.6,"pb_trailing":1.2,"pb_forward":1.1,"div_yield":2.2,"ps_ratio":3.2,"fcf_to_ev":5.24,"fcf_to_mcap":7.69,"liab_to_assets":53.4,"cash_to_assets":6.3,"current_ratio":1.25,"roe":5.2,"roa":2.4,"moat":{"ticker":"SKM","period":"2026Q2","m1_brand_pricing":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"SK Telecom 作為韓國電信龍頭，擁有極高的品牌知名度與客戶忠誠度，這使其在定價上具備一定的優勢。然而，電信業的價格戰與政府監管限制了其完全的定價權。相較於其他產業，其品牌壁壘相對穩固，但並非無懈可擊。公司在提供差異化服務方面持續投入，試圖透過內容、雲端等加值服務鞏固品牌價值，但核心通訊業務的價格彈性仍受市場結構影響。","comment_en":"As South Korea's leading telecom provider, SK Telecom boasts high brand recognition and customer loyalty, granting it a degree of pricing power. However, price competition within the industry and government regulations limit its absolute pricing authority. Compared to other sectors, its brand moat is relatively solid but not impregnable. The company continuously invests in differentiated services, aiming to bolster brand value through value-added offerings like content and cloud services. Nevertheless, the pricing flexibility of its core communication business remains influenced by market structure."},"m2_patents_regulatory":{"score":6,"comment_zh":"電信業的進入門檻相對較高，涉及頻譜資源的分配與政府特許經營權，SK Telecom 在此方面具有一定的監管壁壘。然而，其專利技術並非像科技巨頭那樣具有顛覆性或獨佔性，核心技術的迭代速度快，專利保護的時效性與廣度相對有限。其優勢更多體現在對現有網絡基礎設施的運營許可與監管合規上，而非透過專利創造獨特競爭優勢。","comment_en":"The telecommunications industry has relatively high entry barriers, involving spectrum allocation and government operating licenses. SK Telecom benefits from these regulatory moats. However, its patented technologies are not as disruptive or exclusive as those of tech giants, and core technologies iterate rapidly, limiting the timeliness and breadth of patent protection. Its advantage lies more in operating licenses and regulatory compliance for existing network infrastructure rather than creating unique competitive advantages through patents."},"m3_high_switching_costs":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"對於一般消費者而言，更換電信營運商涉及號碼攜帶、合約終止費用以及重新適應新服務的麻煩，這些都構成了較高的轉換成本。SK Telecom 透過提供綁約優惠、整合性服務套餐來進一步鎖定客戶。雖然有競爭對手試圖透過更優惠的價格或服務吸引用戶，但大部分用戶仍傾向於維持現狀，這為 SK Telecom 提供了穩定的客戶基礎。","comment_en":"For average consumers, switching telecom providers involves the hassle of number portability, contract termination fees, and adapting to new services, all of which constitute relatively high switching costs. SK Telecom further locks in customers by offering bundled discounts and integrated service packages. Although competitors attempt to attract users with better prices or services, most users prefer to stay put, providing SK Telecom with a stable customer base."},"m4_network_effects":{"score":5,"comment_zh":"電信網絡本身具有一定的網絡效應，即用戶越多，網絡價值越高，尤其是在語音通話和基礎數據傳輸方面。然而，這種效應在現代移動通信中已趨於飽和，且主要體現在基礎設施的覆蓋率和穩定性上，而非用戶間互動產生的病毒式增長。SK Telecom 的網絡效應主要來自於其龐大的用戶基數和廣泛的網絡覆蓋，而非社交媒體般的指數級增長。","comment_en":"Telecom networks inherently possess some network effects, where a larger user base enhances network value, particularly for voice calls and basic data transmission. However, this effect has become saturated in modern mobile communications, primarily manifesting in infrastructure coverage and stability rather than viral growth driven by user interactions. SK Telecom's network effects stem mainly from its large user base and extensive network coverage, not exponential growth like social media."},"m5_cost_advantage_scale":{"score":8,"comment_zh":"作為韓國最大的電信營運商，SK Telecom 在網絡建設、採購和運營方面享有顯著的規模經濟效益。其龐大的用戶基礎攤薄了固定基礎設施的成本，並使其在與設備供應商談判時擁有更強的議價能力。這種成本優勢是其維持市場領導地位和盈利能力的重要因素，尤其是在資本密集型的電信行業。","comment_en":"As South Korea's largest telecom operator, SK Telecom enjoys significant economies of scale in network construction, procurement, and operations. Its vast user base dilutes the costs of fixed infrastructure and strengthens its bargaining power with equipment suppliers. This cost advantage is crucial for maintaining its market leadership and profitability, especially in the capital-intensive telecommunications industry."},"m6_unique_geography_assets":{"score":5,"comment_zh":"SK Telecom 的主要業務集中在韓國市場，其地理優勢體現在對韓國國內市場的深入了解和廣泛的基礎設施佈局。然而，這也意味著其業務擴張的地理範圍有限，缺乏全球性的獨特資產。其競爭優勢主要來自於對國內市場的深耕，而非擁有全球稀缺的地理資源或市場。","comment_en":"SK Telecom's primary operations are concentrated in the South Korean market. Its geographical advantage lies in its deep understanding of the domestic market and extensive infrastructure deployment. However, this also limits its geographical scope for business expansion, lacking global unique assets. Its competitive edge stems mainly from cultivating the domestic market rather than possessing globally scarce geographical resources or markets."},"m7_operational_efficiency":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"SK Telecom 在運營效率方面表現穩健，透過持續的技術升級和網絡優化，有效控制了運營成本。其在 5G 網絡的部署和管理上展現了較高的效率，並積極探索 AI、雲端等新興技術以提升服務交付效率。儘管電信業的資本支出龐大，但公司透過精細化管理和自動化，努力維持較高的運營效率和利潤率。","comment_en":"SK Telecom demonstrates solid operational efficiency, effectively controlling operating costs through continuous technological upgrades and network optimization. It exhibits high efficiency in deploying and managing its 5G network and actively explores emerging technologies like AI and cloud to enhance service delivery. Despite substantial capital expenditures in the telecom sector, the company strives to maintain high operational efficiency and profit margins through meticulous management and automation."},"m8_capital_allocation":{"score":6,"comment_zh":"SK Telecom 在資本配置方面展現了穩健的策略，在維持核心電信業務的同時，積極投資於未來增長領域，如 AI、雲端和內容業務。然而，其 ROE 和 ROA 數據顯示，在傳統電信業務上的資本回報率相對不高，這限制了其在資本配置上的彈性與潛力。公司需要持續優化投資組合，以提升整體資本效率。","comment_en":"SK Telecom exhibits a prudent capital allocation strategy, investing in future growth areas like AI, cloud, and content businesses while maintaining its core telecom operations. However, its ROE and ROA figures indicate relatively modest returns on capital in traditional telecom services, limiting its flexibility and potential in capital allocation. The company needs to continuously optimize its investment portfolio to enhance overall capital efficiency."},"m9_customer_retention":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"如轉換成本維度所述，SK Telecom 在客戶保留方面表現出色。透過提供差異化的服務套餐、忠誠度計劃以及不斷提升的網絡質量和客戶服務，公司成功地維持了高客戶留存率。其品牌影響力與服務的穩定性是客戶持續選擇其服務的重要原因，有效抵禦了部分市場競爭壓力。","comment_en":"As mentioned in the switching costs dimension, SK Telecom excels in customer retention. By offering differentiated service packages, loyalty programs, and continuously improving network quality and customer service, the company successfully maintains a high customer retention rate. Its brand influence and service stability are key reasons for customers to continue choosing its services, effectively fending off some market competitive pressures."},"m10_durability":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"電信服務作為現代社會的基礎設施，具有較強的持久性。SK Telecom 作為韓國領先的電信營運商，其網絡和客戶基礎在短期內難以被顛覆。然而，技術快速變革（如衛星互聯網、新通信技術的出現）以及監管政策的變化，對其長期持久性構成潛在挑戰。公司需要持續創新以適應不斷變化的技術和市場環境。","comment_en":"Telecom services, as essential infrastructure for modern society, possess strong durability. As South Korea's leading telecom operator, SK Telecom's network and customer base are difficult to disrupt in the short term. However, rapid technological changes (such as the emergence of satellite internet and new communication technologies) and shifts in regulatory policies pose potential challenges to its long-term durability. The company must continuously innovate to adapt to the evolving technological and market landscape."},"overall_moat_verdict_zh":"SK Telecom 在韓國電信市場擁有穩固的護城河，主要體現在其龐大的規模經濟、相對較高的客戶轉換成本以及領先的品牌聲譽。作為基礎設施提供者，其業務具有一定的特許經營性質，並受益於網絡效應和運營效率。然而，電信業的資本密集度高、技術迭代快且監管嚴格，限制了其部分定價權和利潤率的擴張。其護城河雖堅固，但面對新興技術和市場變化的挑戰，仍需持續創新與優化資本配置以維持長期競爭優勢。","overall_moat_verdict_en":"SK Telecom possesses a solid economic moat in the South Korean telecommunications market, primarily driven by its significant economies of scale, relatively high customer switching costs, and leading brand reputation. As an infrastructure provider, its business has characteristics of a regulated utility, benefiting from network effects and operational efficiencies. However, the capital-intensive nature, rapid technological evolution, and strict regulations in the telecom industry limit its pricing power and profit margin expansion. While its moat is robust, SK Telecom must continuously innovate and optimize capital allocation to maintain its long-term competitive advantage against challenges from emerging technologies and market shifts.","evidenceHash":"f197848bbd276c956e183aa4cf2ef69461ceb5b7cb6514f8f694dd01a597e9bc","assessmentPolicy":"buffett-moat-v3","model":"gemini-2.5-flash-lite","provider":"Vertex AI"},"ratingSources":{"moat":{"reason":null},"fScore":{"score":5,"checkedAt":null},"zScore":{"asOfDate":"2025-12-31","period":"FY 2025","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":"z","zone":"distress","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"KRW","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-31T03:29:05.437Z","evidenceHash":"8ed4b420b5a5c182f2de3c85cc0cef8e73d8f6103bf0a856d9b69e1dabb09cda"},"mScore":{"asOfDate":"2025-12-31","period":"FY 2025","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":null,"zone":"clean","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"KRW","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-31T03:29:05.437Z","evidenceHash":"8ed4b420b5a5c182f2de3c85cc0cef8e73d8f6103bf0a856d9b69e1dabb09cda"}},"fin_valuation":{"is_financial":false},"image":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/SKM.png","logo":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/SKM.png","website":"https://www.sktelecom.com","ceo":"Jai Hun Jung","full_time_employees":"5316","description":"SK Telecom Co., Ltd. operates as a leading provider of wireless telecommunication services throughout South Korea. Its multifaceted operations are structured into three principal segments: Cellular Services, Fixed-Line Telecommunications Services, and Other Businesses. The Cellular Services segment provides a comprehensive suite of offerings, including wireless voice and data transmission, innovative Internet of Things (IoT) solutions, cloud services, and smart factory technologies. It also develops platform-based and subscription services, hosts metaverse platforms, and retails wireless devices. Under Fixed-Line Telecommunications, the company delivers traditional fixed-line telephone connections, high-speed broadband internet, and media platforms such as Internet Protocol TV (IPTV) and cable television, alongside business communication solutions. The Other Businesses segment includes its T-commerce brand for television shopping and various portal services. Beyond these core areas, SK Telecom engages in a wide array of specialized services. These include managing call centers, maintaining base station infrastructure, providing information gathering and consulting, developing and supplying system software, and advancing quantum information and communications technologies. The company also handles database and internet website services, procures digital content, produces and distributes e-books, and sells mastering quality sound albums and other content. Additionally, it trades anti-theft and surveillance equipment and oversees information and communications facilities. As of December 31, 2021, SK Telecom served a substantial customer base, comprising 31.9 million wireless subscribers and 3.6 million fixed-line telephone users. Founded in 1984, this Seoul, South Korea-headquartered company continues to be a prominent player in the telecommunications sector.","description_en":"SK Telecom Co., Ltd. operates as a leading provider of wireless telecommunication services throughout South Korea. Its multifaceted operations are structured into three principal segments: Cellular Services, Fixed-Line Telecommunications Services, and Other Businesses. The Cellular Services segment provides a comprehensive suite of offerings, including wireless voice and data transmission, innovative Internet of Things (IoT) solutions, cloud services, and smart factory technologies. It also develops platform-based and subscription services, hosts metaverse platforms, and retails wireless devices. Under Fixed-Line Telecommunications, the company delivers traditional fixed-line telephone connections, high-speed broadband internet, and media platforms such as Internet Protocol TV (IPTV) and cable television, alongside business communication solutions. The Other Businesses segment includes its T-commerce brand for television shopping and various portal services. Beyond these core areas, SK Telecom engages in a wide array of specialized services. These include managing call centers, maintaining base station infrastructure, providing information gathering and consulting, developing and supplying system software, and advancing quantum information and communications technologies. The company also handles database and internet website services, procures digital content, produces and distributes e-books, and sells mastering quality sound albums and other content. Additionally, it trades anti-theft and surveillance equipment and oversees information and communications facilities. As of December 31, 2021, SK Telecom served a substantial customer base, comprising 31.9 million wireless subscribers and 3.6 million fixed-line telephone users. Founded in 1984, this Seoul, South Korea-headquartered company continues to be a prominent player in the telecommunications sector.","description_zh":"SK Telecom Co.,Ltd（美股代碼：SKM）為 Communication Services 領域之重要企業，專注於 Telecommunications Services 業務，具備清晰之商業壁壘與現金流創造能力。","address":"SK T-Tower","city":"Seoul","state":"SL","zip":"04539","country":"KR","phone":"82 2 6100 2114","full_address":"SK T-Tower, Seoul, SL 04539, KR","range_52w":"19.66-47.18","year_high":47.18,"year_low":19.66,"all_time_high":0,"all_time_low":19.66,"inst_ownership_pct":null,"insider_ownership_pct":null,"top